@* ============ FAQ ============ *@
<section id="faq">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="text-center mb-5">
            <span class="eyebrow d-block mb-2">FAQ for procurement &amp; IT</span>
            <h2 class="display-custom mb-3">The questions that come up before the order.</h2>
            <p class="lead-muted mx-auto" style="max-width: 620px;">
                Everything procurement, legal, and IT want to know before sign-off.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="row justify-content-center">
            <div class="col-lg-10">
                <div class="accordion" id="faqAccordion">

                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button"
                                    data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq1">
                                Can we pay by invoice (purchase order)?
                            </button>
                        </h2>
                        <div id="faq1" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                Yes. For Enterprise and Bundle licenses we issue standard invoices with VAT –
                                made out to your company name, with PO number and 30-day net payment terms.
                                Contact us via the
                                <a href="#" @onclick:preventDefault @onclick='() => ContactSales("Invoice / PO")'>sales form</a>
                                with your billing address, VAT ID, and PO number, and the invoice will arrive by email.
                                For individual purchases via Paddle, the invoice is available in your dashboard
                                immediately after checkout.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button"
                                    data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq2">
                                Is there an MSA or DPA available?
                            </button>
                        </h2>
                        <div id="faq2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                Yes. On request we provide a <strong>Master Service Agreement (MSA)</strong> and a
                                <strong>Data Processing Agreement (DPA) per GDPR Art. 28</strong>.
                                Because running with Ollama processes no personal data at all, an on-prem
                                deployment often doesn't require a DPA – and when using cloud providers with your
                                own API key, the data processing is between you and your chosen AI vendor.
                                Custom contracts and NDAs are possible.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button"
                                    data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq3">
                                Where is our data processed?
                            </button>
                        </h2>
                        <div id="faq3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                You decide. There are three modes:
                                <br><br>
                                <strong>1. Local (Ollama)</strong> – Code and translations stay entirely on your
                                machine or server. No external calls, no telemetry. Ideal for air-gapped
                                environments and regulated industries.
                                <br><br>
                                <strong>2. Cloud with your API key</strong> – Requests go directly from your
                                machine to your AI provider (OpenAI, Azure OpenAI EU, Anthropic). We never see
                                the data. Billing runs through your existing contract.
                                <br><br>
                                <strong>3. Hybrid</strong> – Sensitive resources locally, non-critical ones in the
                                cloud. Configurable per project or per file.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button"
                                    data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq4">
                                What happens after purchase – how do we get the license keys?
                            </button>
                        </h2>
                        <div id="faq4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                After successful payment (via Paddle or invoice) you receive automatically,
                                <strong>within minutes</strong>:
                                <br><br>
                                • The <strong>license key</strong> by email (format
                                <code>EMN-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX</code>)<br>
                                • Access to the <strong>user dashboard</strong> with all licenses and invoices<br>
                                • An <strong>onboarding email</strong> with quickstart instructions<br>
                                • For Enterprise: a proposed slot for the 1:1 onboarding session<br><br>
                                The key is set once in the NuGet package or as an environment variable, and
                                covers all team members on your account.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button"
                                    data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq5">
                                Can we integrate the tools into our CI/CD pipeline?
                            </button>
                        </h2>
                        <div id="faq5" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                Yes – that's exactly what the Enterprise licenses are for. Ready-made integrations
                                exist for <strong>GitHub Actions</strong>, <strong>Azure DevOps</strong>,
                                <strong>GitLab CI</strong>, and generic <strong>MSBuild targets</strong>.
                                The tools run headless, read their configuration from
                                <code>resx.config.json</code> or <code>unittest.config.json</code>, and can act as
                                a quality gate (e.g., fail the build if coverage target isn't met).
                                <br><br>
                                For air-gapped setups we recommend Ollama in the runner – that way no byte
                                leaves your network.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>


@* ============ CONTACT SALES MODAL ============ *@
<div class="modal fade" id="salesModal" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog modal-dialog-centered">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header border-0 pb-0">
                <h5 class="modal-title fw-bold">Contact sales</h5>
                <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button>
            </div>

            <div class="modal-body pt-2">
                <p class="text-secondary small mb-4">
                    We'll get back to you within one business day – with concrete answers, not marketing.
                </p>

                <EditForm Model="salesModel" OnValidSubmit="SubmitSales">
                    <DataAnnotationsValidator />

                    <div class="row g-3">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <label for="salesName" class="form-label">Name *</label>
                            <InputText id="salesName" class="form-control" @bind-Value="salesModel.Name" />
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <label for="salesCompany" class="form-label">Company *</label>
                            <InputText id="salesCompany" class="form-control" @bind-Value="salesModel.Company" />
                        </div>

                        <div class="col-12">
                            <label for="salesEmail" class="form-label">Work email *</label>
                            <InputText id="salesEmail" type="email" class="form-control" @bind-Value="salesModel.Email" />
                        </div>

                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <label for="salesTeamSize" class="form-label">Team size</label>
                            <InputSelect id="salesTeamSize" class="form-select" @bind-Value="salesModel.TeamSize">
                                <option value="1-5">1 – 5 developers</option>
                                <option value="6-20">6 – 20 developers</option>
                                <option value="21-50">21 – 50 developers</option>
                                <option value="51+">51+ developers</option>
                            </InputSelect>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <label for="salesDeployment" class="form-label">Deployment</label>
                            <InputSelect id="salesDeployment" class="form-select" @bind-Value="salesModel.Deployment">
                                <option value="cloud">Cloud (API key)</option>
                                <option value="ollama">On-prem (Ollama)</option>
                                <option value="hybrid">Hybrid</option>
                                <option value="unsure">Not sure yet</option>
                            </InputSelect>
                        </div>

                        <div class="col-12">
                            <label for="salesMessage" class="form-label">Message</label>
                            <InputTextArea id="salesMessage" class="form-control" rows="3"
                                           placeholder="What's it about? (e.g., PO, DPA, onboarding, custom licensing)"
                                           @bind-Value="salesModel.Message" />
                        </div>

                        <div class="col-12 mt-4">
                            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-brand w-100 btn-lg-custom">
                                Send request
                            </button>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <p class="text-secondary small text-center mt-3 mb-0">
                        By submitting, you agree that we may contact you to handle this inquiry.
                        No data shared with third parties.
                    </p>
                </EditForm>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>